# The reads outside we_read.c that still open a name themselves.  Checked by
# tests/check-read-owner.sh.
#
#   file|r22x:function|count|pass|reason
#
# x is the clause letter (a fopen, b open, c a folder listing, d fdopen, e a
# library that opens a file, f getline, g a request with no bound, k an
# object's imported opener, z an open token that is not a call); for clause k
# the file is the object and the function the symbol.  "count" may only fall,
# and a line that matches nothing is stale.  "pass" is the pass that moves the
# site onto the owner and deletes the line (P2 the assistant's reads, P3a the
# plain callers, P3b the load of a pipe, P3c Find in files); a pass ending in
# /cfg is a row only some configurations meet, so a build without it is not
# stale.  "keep" is a permanent row, and the reason says why the name is the
# editor's own and not one a user, a folder, a model or a server chose.

# the plain callers (P3a)
we_ai.c|r22a:ai_read_first_line|1|P3a|the user's key file
we_debug.c|r22a:e_lsp_read_file_text|1|P3a|a file a language server named
we_fileop.c|r22b:fileop_open_source|1|P3a|moves onto wpe_read_open with the walk's folder descriptor
we_fl_fkt.c|r22a:e_i_fopen|4|P3a|help and info files by name
we_fl_fkt.c|r22e:e_i_fopen|6|P3a|gzopen of help and info files by name
we_fl_fkt.o|r22k:gzopen|1|P3a/cfg|e_i_fopen, in a build with zlib
we_fl_unix.c|r22a:WpeHandleFileManager|1|P3a|the probe of Block > Read and the other modes
we_fl_unix.c|r22c:fm_folder_has_entries|1|P3a|the File Manager lists a folder
we_fl_unix.o|r22k:opendir|1|P3a|fm_folder_has_entries
we_main.c|r22a:e_read_whole|1|P3a|the migration of an old configuration
we_opt.c|r22a:e_read_help_str|1|P3a|help.key from the installed folder
we_prog.c|r22a:e_algol68_sniff|1|P3a|the first lines of the window's file
we_startcmd.c|r22b:startcmd_open_store|1|P3a|the editor's own store, until it is on the owner
we_startcmd.c|r22d:startcmd_stream_of|1|P3a|fdopen of the store's descriptor, for reading and for writing
we_startcmd.c|r22f:built_read_stream|1|P3a|the editor's own store, until it is on the owner
we_startcmd.c|r22f:startcmd_parse_stream|1|P3a|the editor's own store, until it is on the owner
we_startplan.c|r22b:startplan_is_build_output|1|P3a|a private copy of the owner's open
we_startplan.c|r22b:startplan_read_startup|1|P3a|a private copy of the owner's open
we_startplan.c|r22b:wpe_startplan_elf_section|1|P3a|the user's program, read by section
we_unix.c|r22c:e_find_dir|1|P3a|the File Manager lists a folder
we_unix.c|r22c:e_find_files|1|P3a|the File Manager lists a folder
we_unix.o|r22k:opendir|1|P3a|e_find_dir and e_find_files
WeSyntax.c|r22a:WpeSyntaxOpenPersonal|1|P3a|the user's syntax_def
WeSyntax.c|r22a:WpeSyntaxOpenSystem|1|P3a|the installed syntax_def
WeXterm.c|r22e:WpeXDefaults|1|P3a|XrmGetFileDatabase of ~/.Xdefaults

# the load of a pipe (P3b) and Find in files (P3c)
we_edit.c|r22a:e_edit_open|1|P3b|File > Open and the command line
we_fl_unix.c|r22a:WpeGrepFile|1|P3c|every entry of a folder

# not a name a user, a folder, a model or a server chose
we_debug.c|r22a:e_d_compile_show_errors|1|keep|a file the editor wrote in its own 0700 temporary folder
we_debug.c|r22a:e_d_debugger_pid_read|1|keep|a file the editor wrote in its own 0700 temporary folder
we_debug.c|r22b:e_d_script_connect|4|keep|the debugger's own pipes and terminal, in the editor's 0700 temporary folder
we_debug.c|r22c:e_find_supported_jdk|1|keep|lists fixed system folders for a JDK and opens no file
we_debug.o|r22k:glob|1|keep|e_find_supported_jdk
we_fl_fkt.c|r22c:e_tmp_remove|1|keep|removes the editor's own temporary folder without following links
we_fl_fkt.o|r22k:nftw|1|keep|e_tmp_remove
we_opt.c|r22f:e_opt_read_line|1|keep|its stream is the owner's memory stream of at most 1 MiB
we_prog.c|r22g:e_check_header|1|keep|reads 120 bytes at a time with constant memory and a regular file ends; a bound in memory would remove the only brake the include recursion has
we_progn.c|r22g:e_aopen_stream|1|keep|reads a line at a time with constant memory and a regular file ends
we_write.c|r22b:write_backup_source|1|keep|the write owner's own judged open of the file it backs up
we_write.c|r22b:write_mode_open_descriptor|1|keep|the write owner's own judged open for the mode

